  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "政治社會學：分配正義",
    "sub_ename": "POLITICAL SOCIOLOGY：DISTRIBUTIVE JUSTICE",
    "describe_ch": "政治是權威性的價值分配。這句政治學學的經典名言，闡述了資源分配的緣由。誰獲得？誰失去？因此，我們必須思考：「什麼是正義」。\n當代的台灣，我們對意識形態給予了太多負面的評價，也導致對於「左」與「「右」缺乏認識。這進一步影響了一系列關於基本人權的思考。\n本課程從左翼社會民主出發，思考更多「社會投資」的可能性，思考人類社會將在競爭中尋求生存？或是具有「共生」的可能性。",
    "describe_eh": "“ Politics as the authoritative allocation of values for the society”.This classic phrase from political science explains the reasons for resource allocation. Who gets it? who loses? Therefore, we must think: \"What is the justice\"?\nIn contemporary Taiwan, we have given too many negative evaluations of ideology, which has also led to a lack of understanding of \"leftists\" and \"rightists\".\nStarting from left-wing social democracy, this course considers the possibility of more \"social investment\", and considers whether human society will seek survival in competition? Or have the possibility of \"symbiosis\".",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 2.0
  },
